# End-to-end EMULATOR test: synthetic SAMD21G18 (Cortex-M0+) printer
# under Renode in tick mode. No shipped config/ board exists for this
# chip, so this is the SAMD21 per-printer test in spirit: a
# realistically-shaped cartesian pin map driven through the same
# TMC-UART + ADC infrastructure the real-board tests use, where
# samd21_smoke covers boot only. Clock is TC4-driven; host link is
# SERCOM0 on PA10/PA11. See "Per-printer tests" in
# test/emulator/README.md for the shared conventions.
#
# Ground specific to this chip:
#   - TMC2209 multi-drop UART (uart_pin PA6 / tx_pin PA7, uart_address
#     0..3). sw_uart._drive_rx drives the firmware RX bit through the
#     SAMD21 PORT model (gpio_a.OnGPIO). First SAMD-family sw_uart
#     test, so it also covers the renode_hooks CPU resolver accepting
#     `cpu0` (the SAMD repls' name) as well as `cpu`.
#   - samd21_adc_stub.py: the SAMD21 ADC register map differs from the
#     SAMX5 one. Hotend reads channel index 4 (PA4), bed index 5 (PA5).
#     A broken ADC sits at temp=0.0 with no shutdown, so the temp=3
#     assertion below is the positive proof samples arrived.
DICTIONARY samd21g18.dict
CONFIG samd21_printer.cfg
EMULATOR samd21_printer.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x21"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "temp=3"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
